James sought feedback on a line he wrote regarding the increase in extreme weather events and its economic implications. He received advice to ensure accuracy and nuance, referencing the IPCC's findings. Suggestions were made to incorporate previous climate predictions and to include citations for credibility. James then considered adding a structural overview of the report in the introduction, outlining major chapters on macroeconomic risks, the case for adaptation investment, and a call for action on adaptation investment. The final version recommended integrating citations seamlessly and providing a clear roadmap of the report’s structure at the end of the introduction.
